00:25:19.140 --> 00:25:21.480
And then maybe go be chatty with Jim about it later.

492
00:25:21.880 --> 00:25:26.320
But instead, Pam points at the screen and goes, wait, is that Jan?

493
00:25:26.700 --> 00:25:27.700
That's Jan.

494
00:25:27.700 --> 00:25:31.460
And I feel like that's something Michael or Dwight would have done normally.

495
00:25:32.560 --> 00:25:34.260
I totally hear that.

496
00:25:34.260 --> 00:25:37.340
I think that's a valid analysis.

497
00:25:37.480 --> 00:25:43.180
I will say, I think it was probably so shocking to Pam that she just blurted it out.

498
00:25:43.400 --> 00:25:46.580
I mean, it's to see Jan in the picture.

499
00:25:46.840 --> 00:25:50.120
She just, I imagine she was just like, oh my God.

500
00:25:51.180 --> 00:25:52.660
Okay, okay, fair enough.

501
00:25:52.840 --> 00:25:53.500
Okay, I get it.

502
00:25:53.620 --> 00:25:56.880
Well, we had a fan question about this scene, Angela, from Maren Allen.

503
00:25:57.220 --> 00:26:02.760
She wrote in to say, my 13-year-old daughter Dakota pointed out that when Pam notices Jan

504
00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:08.700
and Michael's vacation slideshow, Michael says that she's actually a German woman named

505
00:26:08.700 --> 00:26:09.480
Ergel Gru.

506
00:26:09.840 --> 00:26:15.880
And my daughter would like to know if this name was improvised and if it has anything to do

507
00:26:15.880 --> 00:26:20.260
with Steve's Despicable Me character, Gru, I had the same question.

508
00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:21.940
So I looked it up.

509
00:26:22.220 --> 00:26:26.760
This episode was filmed in 2007, back from vacation.

510
00:26:27.500 --> 00:26:29.860
Despicable Me came out in 2010.

511
00:26:30.020 --> 00:26:35.660
So then I researched animation production and how long it takes a movie like Despicable Me

512
00:26:35.660 --> 00:26:38.660
to be made, and they take three to five years.

513
00:26:39.120 --> 00:26:46.380
So it is possible that there was an overlap that Steve was doing voiceover while we were

514
00:26:46.380 --> 00:26:47.520
filming on The Office.

515
00:26:47.520 --> 00:26:48.460
It's possible.

516
00:26:48.680 --> 00:26:49.940
Oh my gosh.

517
00:26:49.940 --> 00:26:57.460
And maybe that is why, because in the script it says Erlgra, but he says Erkel Gru.

518
00:26:58.060 --> 00:27:02.560
Maybe it was like on his mind, and that's why he said Gru.

519
00:27:02.900 --> 00:27:04.120
Let's move it on.

520
00:27:04.120 --> 00:27:09.440
And Michael, I mean, he's got to tell someone, right?

521
00:27:09.700 --> 00:27:16.180
He's so excited to tell Packer that Jan went with him to Jamaica, and Packer doesn't believe

522
00:27:16.180 --> 00:27:16.380
him.

523
00:27:16.500 --> 00:27:17.240
He's like, no way.

524
00:27:17.480 --> 00:27:18.940
So Michael's like, you know what?

525
00:27:18.940 --> 00:27:19.840
I'll send you a picture.

526
00:27:21.380 --> 00:27:25.540
And Packer's email is Packer at Dunder Mifflin.

527
00:27:26.320 --> 00:27:30.300
But he sends it to Packaging at Dunder Mifflin.

528
00:27:30.520 --> 00:27:33.700
And how this all goes down in the scene is so great.

529
00:27:34.220 --> 00:27:36.580
Because Michael is like, did you get it?

530
00:27:36.740 --> 00:27:37.460
Hit refresh.

531
00:27:37.820 --> 00:27:38.360
Hit refresh.

532
00:27:38.940 --> 00:27:41.300
And Packer is like, no, I didn't get it.

533
00:27:41.420 --> 00:27:45.160
And then all of a sudden he says, oh, I just got it from someone else.

534
00:27:46.720 --> 00:27:49.140
And then Michael's like, wait, wait, what?

535
00:27:49.300 --> 00:27:49.860
Who else?

536
00:27:50.020 --> 00:27:50.260
What?

537
00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:54.380
And then Michael realizes he has sent it to the wrong place.

538
00:27:54.540 --> 00:27:56.360
He sent it to Daryl in the warehouse.

539
00:27:56.740 --> 00:28:02.640
Who has clearly forwarded it to Packer or someone else who forwarded it to Packer.

540
00:28:02.760 --> 00:28:04.500
But it is out, basically.

541
00:28:05.300 --> 00:28:10.920
I want to point out that that line at the end when Packer says, how do I get you out

542
00:28:10.920 --> 00:28:11.560
of this picture?

543
00:28:12.080 --> 00:28:13.120
That was an improv.

544
00:28:13.460 --> 00:28:15.100
That was a Dave Koechner ad.

545
00:28:15.340 --> 00:28:17.560
Yeah, that's Dave Koechner at his beSt.

546
00:28:17.860 --> 00:28:21.500
After Michael gets off the phone with Packer, he is freaked out.

547
00:28:21.700 --> 00:28:23.360
Oh, he's freaking the heck out.

548
00:28:23.360 --> 00:28:25.520
He needs to do damage control.

549
00:28:25.820 --> 00:28:27.400
So he runs.

550
00:28:27.620 --> 00:28:30.120
He sprints to the warehouse.

551
00:28:30.560 --> 00:28:32.780
We had a fan question from Anna Rhodes.

552
00:28:33.100 --> 00:28:38.160
She says, at 7 minutes, 20 seconds, where is that hallway that Michael is running down

553
00:28:38.160 --> 00:28:39.180
to get to the warehouse?

554
00:28:39.820 --> 00:28:41.620
Anna, I had the same question.

555
00:28:41.620 --> 00:28:44.440
So I did some digging, but Jenna, I know you did too.

556
00:28:44.600 --> 00:28:45.860
And you went to Kentopedia.

557
00:28:46.120 --> 00:28:46.840
So what do you got?

558
00:28:47.440 --> 00:28:48.040
All right.

559
00:28:48.240 --> 00:28:52.580
Kent told me that that is the hallway where our writers work.

560
00:28:52.580 --> 00:28:55.400
He is running down the writer's hallway.

561
00:28:55.740 --> 00:28:58.300
All those doors you see are writers' offices.

562
00:28:58.580 --> 00:29:03.540
And when he turns the corner and he runs through that doorway, he is running into Mindy

563
00:29:03.540 --> 00:29:04.580
Kaling's office.

564
00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:05.860
Is he really?

565
00:29:06.200 --> 00:29:06.660
Yes.

566
00:29:06.920 --> 00:29:07.320
Oh, my God.

567
00:29:07.380 --> 00:29:08.900
I thought that was Kent's office.

568
00:29:09.180 --> 00:29:09.980
Oh, my gosh.

569
00:29:10.060 --> 00:29:10.860
OK, I love that.

570
00:29:11.280 --> 00:29:12.940
Well, I have a little catch, Jenna.

571
00:29:13.960 --> 00:29:17.400
He runs past a woman sitting at a desk, right?

572
00:29:17.620 --> 00:29:19.280
Right at the very beginning of his sprint.

573
00:29:19.500 --> 00:29:21.240
Well, that is Mary Wall.

574
00:29:21.240 --> 00:29:23.740
And she was our executive producer assistant.

575
00:29:23.980 --> 00:29:25.420
She's in an orange hoodie.

576
00:29:25.940 --> 00:29:27.320
She was the beSt.

577
00:29:27.480 --> 00:29:28.800
She did everything for us.

578
00:29:28.900 --> 00:29:31.460
I love that we put Mary in that scene.

579
00:29:31.600 --> 00:29:34.600
So I guess they just made all the writers close their doors.

580
00:29:35.060 --> 00:29:36.900
But they let Mary keep working.

581
00:29:36.900 --> 00:29:38.340
And they just shot that scene.

582
00:29:38.480 --> 00:29:39.480
Steve ran right past her.

583
00:29:39.480 --> 00:29:39.900
Yeah.

584
00:29:40.060 --> 00:29:45.080
And the desk that Mary is sitting at is directly outside of the writer's room conference room.

585
00:29:45.300 --> 00:29:46.700
They had their own conference room.

586
00:29:46.820 --> 00:29:52.040
And Steve starts his sprint right in the doorway of that writer's room conference room.

587
00:29:52.140 --> 00:29:54.720
And he runs right past Mary at the desk outside of it.

588
00:29:54.860 --> 00:29:58.760
Well, after he runs into Mindy's office, obviously, it's a dead end.

589
00:29:58.760 --> 00:30:00.400
So they had to cut there.

590
00:30:00.980 --> 00:30:10.380
Then Steve had to go down into the warehouse, walk up the steps, and get into that little fake box at the top of the stairs that actually leads nowhere.

591
00:30:11.120 --> 00:30:12.760
And then come back down.

592
00:30:13.260 --> 00:30:13.780
Yes.

593
00:30:13.780 --> 00:30:20.620
And then they would yell, action, and he would come running back down the stairs as if he had actually come from somewhere.

594
00:30:21.180 --> 00:30:21.340
Right.

595
00:30:22.200 --> 00:30:24.760
So then he runs into Daryl's office.

596
00:30:24.760 --> 00:30:32.000
And I believe, Angela, this is the first time we've seen Daryl's office in the warehouse, where we've actually gone inside of it.

597
00:30:32.120 --> 00:30:38.240
In this scene, at 7 minutes 38 seconds, Daryl is eating a giant plate of food.

598
00:30:38.240 --> 00:30:42.120
We had a fan question from Dave H.

599
00:30:42.300 --> 00:30:43.880
and Andrea Petit-Bell.

600
00:30:44.640 --> 00:30:50.380
What is up with Daryl's massive plate of food when Michael goes in to ask him about the picture?

601
00:30:50.640 --> 00:30:54.880
Well, Angela, it is not in the script that Daryl is eating.

602
00:30:55.260 --> 00:30:57.340
And usually it is.

603
00:30:57.520 --> 00:30:59.360
Usually it is scripted that we're eating food.

604
00:31:00.200 --> 00:31:01.800
Here's why I went to look.

605
00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:07.640
When I looked at that plate of food, it 100% looked like the stuff they would serve us at craft services.

606
00:31:07.640 --> 00:31:09.380
I thought the same thing.

607
00:31:09.700 --> 00:31:10.840
Jenna, oh, my God.

608
00:31:11.020 --> 00:31:16.640
When I looked at it, I was like, is Craig, as Daryl, just holding his lunch?

609
00:31:16.940 --> 00:31:18.660
Or like a snack he made?

610
00:31:19.400 --> 00:31:19.840
Yeah.

611
00:31:20.120 --> 00:31:27.660
I think he was hungry and he was having a plate of food and they were like, oh, you should just eat that in the scene.

612
00:31:27.820 --> 00:31:29.620
That food brought me back.

613
00:31:29.800 --> 00:31:31.940
I had a sense memory when I saw the plate.

614
00:31:32.200 --> 00:31:33.660
I was like, that's our food.

615
00:31:33.780 --> 00:31:35.240
That's what we used to eat all the time.

616
00:31:35.240 --> 00:31:39.180
Yeah, especially like they would bring in those big trays of chicken wings.

617
00:31:39.380 --> 00:31:39.560
Remember?

618
00:31:39.800 --> 00:31:40.040
Yes.

619
00:31:40.280 --> 00:31:41.780
Like drumsticks and wings.

620
00:31:41.900 --> 00:31:42.200
Yes.

621
00:31:42.380 --> 00:31:47.280
Well, so when Michael is there, he's asking Daryl, did you get my email?

622
00:31:47.560 --> 00:31:47.920
Did you?

623
00:31:48.340 --> 00:31:49.560
And Daryl's like, yeah.

624
00:31:49.760 --> 00:31:52.540
And he's like, well, did you get my email about deleting that email?

625
00:31:52.740 --> 00:31:54.200
And Daryl's like, you know what, Mike?

626
00:31:54.260 --> 00:31:55.820
I'm very busy down here.

627
00:31:56.120 --> 00:32:01.080
So clearly Daryl is going to be no help in getting Michael's picture deleted.

628
00:32:01.080 --> 00:32:02.200
Oh, no.

629
00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:05.820
Well, I want to take us back to accounting for a second, Jenna.

630
00:32:06.180 --> 00:32:08.120
Humor me for some background catches.

631
00:32:08.500 --> 00:32:16.000
At 8 minutes, 12 seconds, Andy, Meredith and Jim are gathered around Kevin's computer looking at the photo.

632
00:32:16.500 --> 00:32:23.980
Now, over Kevin's shoulder, you can see a message on his bulletin board that says, don't eat the yellow snow.

633
00:32:24.560 --> 00:32:27.720
So maybe Kevin needed a reminder.

634
00:32:28.400 --> 00:32:34.140
But at 8 minutes, 18 seconds, there is a post-it note on Angela Martin's side of the partition.

635
00:32:34.420 --> 00:32:37.580
And Jenna, I zoomed in on that sucker.

636
00:32:37.760 --> 00:32:39.580
I zoomed on it so hard.

637
00:32:39.580 --> 00:32:40.880
And do you know what it says?

638
00:32:41.060 --> 00:32:43.900
We got so much mail about this post-it note.

639
00:32:44.100 --> 00:32:46.460
Angela, you're going to make so many people very happy right now.

640
00:32:46.620 --> 00:32:47.320
What does it say?

641
00:32:47.560 --> 00:32:53.360
Well, I have to thank my husband, Josh, because this was half an hour of our lives that I made him do with me.

642
00:32:53.920 --> 00:32:55.800
He has editing software.

643
00:32:56.120 --> 00:32:58.020
I made him screen grab, blow it up.

644
00:32:58.140 --> 00:33:00.900
We put different filters on it that would highlight different letters.

645
00:33:01.180 --> 00:33:05.200
You guys, it was a huge task, but we did it.

646
00:33:05.780 --> 00:33:11.360
This is what we 99.9% believe that it says after our half an hour research.

647
00:33:11.920 --> 00:33:17.760
Angela, can I have $8 petty cash to buy some more jelly beans?

648
00:33:18.060 --> 00:33:20.000
I'll get you licorice and cherry.

649
00:33:20.360 --> 00:33:20.860
Thanks, Pam.

650
00:33:21.080 --> 00:33:22.460
Oh, my gosh.

651
00:33:22.460 --> 00:33:24.860
I'll get you licorice and cherry.

652
00:33:25.440 --> 00:33:27.560
Well, you know that Dwight likes licorice.

653
00:33:27.800 --> 00:33:28.200
Wow.

654
00:33:28.440 --> 00:33:30.040
I guess you're the one who likes cherry.

655
00:33:30.220 --> 00:33:31.020
I guess so.

656
00:33:31.180 --> 00:33:34.860
But we literally, it was like we had found the Rosetta Stone.

657
00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:35.820
We're like, that's an R.

658
00:33:35.940 --> 00:33:36.580
I'm positive.

659
00:33:36.960 --> 00:33:37.980
Okay, that's a C.

660
00:33:38.200 --> 00:33:39.240
That's a Y.

661
00:33:39.240 --> 00:33:46.760
Like, literally, like we were like figuring out hieroglyphics and we became obsessed.

662
00:33:46.940 --> 00:33:48.920
And that's what we're pretty sure it says.

663
00:33:49.260 --> 00:33:54.020
Well, what I love about that is that it reveals that Pam doesn't pay for her own candy.

664
00:33:54.720 --> 00:34:00.680
She gets petty cash from Angela and that it is something that Pam is doing for the office,

665
00:34:00.880 --> 00:34:03.280
almost like maybe the person before her did it, too.

666
00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:07.960
I could imagine Pam starting work and Angela going up to her and saying, you will put out

667
00:34:07.960 --> 00:34:09.000
candy on your desk.

668
00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:11.040
I will give you petty cash.

669
00:34:11.580 --> 00:34:13.080
You need to bring me a receipt.

670
00:34:13.540 --> 00:34:17.300
But like this is part of Pam's like work liSt.

671
00:34:17.840 --> 00:34:22.040
Yeah, it made me rethink front reception, too, especially during the holidays, because I

672
00:34:22.040 --> 00:34:26.320
thought all those little decorations, I always sort of thought that was Pam's effort to spruce

673
00:34:26.320 --> 00:34:27.280
up her desk area.

674
00:34:27.460 --> 00:34:32.220
But now I think maybe Angela Martin is like, remember, you have a budget for decorating the

675
00:34:32.220 --> 00:34:32.760
front reception.

676
00:34:32.960 --> 00:34:35.000
It's the first thing people see when they walk through the door.

677
00:34:35.780 --> 00:34:38.720
Yeah, like this candy and the decorations are mandated.

678
00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:41.780
Can we, though, believe that Pam buys the plants herself?

679
00:34:42.740 --> 00:34:43.920
If you want to.

680
00:34:44.600 --> 00:34:44.960
Thanks.

681
00:34:46.180 --> 00:34:49.080
She can't keep any of them alive, but OK.

682
00:34:50.100 --> 00:34:50.620
OK.

683
00:34:50.860 --> 00:34:51.300
All right.

684
00:34:51.480 --> 00:34:53.500
So now we have two things happening.

685
00:34:54.160 --> 00:34:57.500
We have Michael, who tells Dwight about the photo.

686
00:34:58.300 --> 00:35:00.920
He says he needs Dwight's help in retrieving it.

687
00:35:01.080 --> 00:35:05.460
My favorite part of this scene is when we learn that Michael has named the photo Jamaican

688
00:35:05.460 --> 00:35:06.600
Jan's son princess.

689
00:35:06.600 --> 00:35:06.780
Yes.

690
00:35:07.320 --> 00:35:07.540
Amazing.

691
00:35:07.960 --> 00:35:11.100
And then the other thing that happens is that Jim is sad.

692
00:35:11.320 --> 00:35:13.080
Sad Jim is in the break room.

693
00:35:13.640 --> 00:35:14.500
Pam walks in.

694
00:35:15.320 --> 00:35:17.740
And she gets Jim to confide in her.

695
00:35:18.160 --> 00:35:21.740
And he says that he is in kind of a stupid fight with Karen.

696
00:35:22.400 --> 00:35:24.760
And Pam says, do you want to talk about it?

697
00:35:24.920 --> 00:35:25.900
I have a question for you.

698
00:35:26.500 --> 00:35:26.900
What?

699
00:35:27.120 --> 00:35:29.900
Do you really think that Pam wants to talk about it?

700
00:35:30.020 --> 00:35:36.000
Or do you think somewhere deep in her subconscious, I don't think she's a mean-spirited person,

701
00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:40.540
but maybe she has found a way just to spend time with him again?

702
00:35:41.340 --> 00:35:42.300
Of course.

703
00:35:43.260 --> 00:35:44.180
Of course.

704
00:35:44.720 --> 00:35:47.320
She has ulterior motives here.

705
00:35:48.080 --> 00:35:52.680
Well, I think it's also, though, you know what?

706
00:35:52.720 --> 00:35:55.140
I actually don't think she has those ulterior motives.

707
00:35:55.380 --> 00:36:01.900
I think she is really trying to believe and convince herself that she can have a friendship

708
00:36:01.900 --> 00:36:04.740
with Jim and that this is what friends do.

709
00:36:05.080 --> 00:36:08.260
So, yes, I think part of her is craving that connection.

710
00:36:08.460 --> 00:36:14.320
But I think the real thing and why she's going to break down later is that she thinks she's

711
00:36:14.320 --> 00:36:16.280
ready to be this kind of friend to him.

712
00:36:17.400 --> 00:36:19.580
And she's going to find out that she's not.

713
00:36:19.720 --> 00:36:20.080
Right.

714
00:36:20.300 --> 00:36:21.420
But she thinks that she is.

715
00:36:21.560 --> 00:36:22.540
And this is her attempt.

716
00:36:22.880 --> 00:36:25.620
Well, I'll tell you, there's a deleted scene between Jim and Pam.

717
00:36:25.820 --> 00:36:30.100
I'm actually, for their storyline, I think it was the right thing to delete it

718
00:36:30.100 --> 00:36:36.620
because it takes Pam's sort of earnestness to want to help him and try to really be a good

719
00:36:36.620 --> 00:36:37.260
friend to him.

720
00:36:37.940 --> 00:36:41.420
And it makes it seem like maybe she just wanted to hang out with him.

721
00:36:41.520 --> 00:36:46.880
And it's the two of you at front reception at Pam's computer, kind of in that canoodling

722
00:36:46.880 --> 00:36:50.540
form, the way you guys used to play in pranks on Dwight and he'd be leaning in.

723
00:36:50.640 --> 00:36:52.080
You'd be laughing and looking at each other.

724
00:36:52.300 --> 00:36:53.880
You're doing all of that.

725
00:36:53.920 --> 00:36:57.120
But you're looking for apartments together for Karen.

726
00:36:57.840 --> 00:37:01.440
Oh, and it felt, it felt off.

727
00:37:01.580 --> 00:37:03.520
And so I think it was the right move to delete it.

728
00:37:04.820 --> 00:37:10.160
I'm glad they deleted that because my takeaway from this episode was that Pam was being really

729
00:37:10.160 --> 00:37:10.620
earneSt.

730
00:37:10.940 --> 00:37:11.340
Yeah.

731
00:37:11.540 --> 00:37:15.760
And then just realized she can't, she, yeah, she can't be that yet.

732
00:37:17.240 --> 00:37:22.460
Well, we also get a big piece of information about Jim and Karen's relationship in the scene.

733
00:37:22.640 --> 00:37:25.320
We find out that they've been dating a month.

734
00:37:26.630 --> 00:37:29.550
Jim says, we've only been dating a month.

735
00:37:29.970 --> 00:37:31.410
That is not very long.

736
00:37:32.330 --> 00:37:32.810
No.

